1
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:46,508
What beautiful weather. Pink cherry blossoms, a blue sky, and fluffy white clouds.

2
00:01:47,288 --> 00:01:51,268
There's nothing like a spring picnic by the water under the cherry trees.

3
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:55,428
Akari, I want to have another waste ball.

4
00:01:55,748 --> 00:01:57,908
Alright then, which one do you want?

5
00:01:57,908 --> 00:02:02,188
Um, Yoshi flakes! And a chicken nugget too!

6
00:02:05,088 --> 00:02:11,068
So many of the petals have fallen already, but it's almost nicer when there are fewer people out here.

7
00:02:11,468 --> 00:02:15,588
You know how crowded it can get, but it's so peaceful now.

8
00:02:16,148 --> 00:02:18,868
I wonder if where's in Yamagata by now?

9
00:02:19,468 --> 00:02:23,208
I don't know, maybe, but I bet it's beautiful there too.

10
00:02:24,468 --> 00:02:26,908
Human Shogi is so creative.

11
00:02:26,908 --> 00:02:31,248
Yeah, they wear kimonos and cool armor and they play it in the park.

12
00:02:31,428 --> 00:02:33,648
I bet it's lovely under the cherry trees.

13
00:02:34,028 --> 00:02:39,248
With the blossoms in full bloom, the beautiful blue sky, and the tall green mountains.

14
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:40,188
How wonderful.

15
00:02:41,148 --> 00:02:44,388
He's so lucky. It sounds so romantic.

16
00:02:44,388 --> 00:02:51,488
No matter where I go, the rain always seems to follow me.

17
00:02:52,008 --> 00:02:54,888
Outdoor festivals and me just don't get along.

18
00:02:55,388 --> 00:02:58,028
Not to mention I'm embarrassed by my straight losses.

19
00:02:58,528 --> 00:03:00,808
I failed to get anywhere in the Shishio tournament.

20
00:03:01,168 --> 00:03:02,808
I couldn't even bring a match here.

21
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:05,048
Damn that chairman.

22
00:03:05,048 --> 00:03:06,708
It'll be fine.

23
00:03:07,128 --> 00:03:07,688
Fine!

24
00:03:07,988 --> 00:03:09,348
Just go and have a good time.

25
00:03:09,468 --> 00:03:11,628
Relax, you worry so much you're going bald.

26
00:03:11,888 --> 00:03:16,168
Oh wait, I guess saying that is pretty taboo, so you can just ignore me.

27
00:03:17,468 --> 00:03:18,948
This is the worst.

28
00:03:20,648 --> 00:03:22,228
Here, let me carry your bag.

29
00:03:22,228 --> 00:03:24,028
Okay, let's get going.

30
00:03:27,868 --> 00:03:29,708
What the hell's with that song?

31
00:03:30,008 --> 00:03:33,848
It sounds so weird echoing through a completely empty train station like that.

32
00:03:34,208 --> 00:03:35,728
Why are they playing this song?

33
00:03:35,828 --> 00:03:37,368
It's just so creepy and sad.

34
00:03:37,368 --> 00:03:48,328
How do I apologize for what happened?

35
00:03:49,148 --> 00:03:50,968
They're all so kind.

36
00:03:52,088 --> 00:03:55,928
And I know they would never blame me for not making it.

37
00:03:57,228 --> 00:03:59,708
But that makes it even more painful.

38
00:04:00,908 --> 00:04:05,328
I think I'd rather be berated by them.

39
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:10,808
Hey, Kai!

40
00:04:11,108 --> 00:04:12,808
You brought the rain again!

41
00:04:13,088 --> 00:04:15,268
Yeah, so what are you going to do about it?

42
00:04:15,308 --> 00:04:16,888
This weather is your fault!

43
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,788
Can't you just leave the rain behind?

44
00:04:19,088 --> 00:04:23,068
That being said, I'm being scolded already.

45
00:04:24,328 --> 00:04:27,828
Here, make yourself useful and hand out towels to the pawns.

46
00:04:27,828 --> 00:04:28,008
Huh?

47
00:04:30,088 --> 00:04:30,968
Here you go.

48
00:04:31,208 --> 00:04:32,248
Please have a towel.

49
00:04:33,108 --> 00:04:34,028
Ishimara Eitan!

50
00:04:34,028 --> 00:04:35,468
Thank you so much!

51
00:04:38,748 --> 00:04:40,408
Here, try this.

52
00:04:40,588 --> 00:04:42,948
It's a new recipe from the Shiono Club.

53
00:04:43,088 --> 00:04:45,208
We call it our pear rice cake.

54
00:04:45,448 --> 00:04:46,228
It's delicious.

55
00:04:46,548 --> 00:04:47,368
It tastes great.

56
00:04:47,688 --> 00:04:48,488
It's wonderful.

57
00:04:49,488 --> 00:04:52,528
Well, I thought we were going to make a bundle selling the new product.

58
00:04:52,948 --> 00:04:55,428
But with this rain, nobody will be coming.

59
00:04:55,568 --> 00:04:56,508
Sorry about that.

60
00:04:57,008 --> 00:04:57,528
Kiriyama!

61
00:04:57,888 --> 00:04:58,668
Mr. Shimada!

62
00:04:58,668 --> 00:05:03,268
Wow, kiddo.

63
00:05:03,768 --> 00:05:04,888
Looking good.

64
00:05:05,168 --> 00:05:05,988
Nice costume.

65
00:05:06,508 --> 00:05:08,688
Looks to me like you were born to wear that.

66
00:05:08,928 --> 00:05:09,388
Wow.

67
00:05:10,048 --> 00:05:12,788
It suits him so perfectly, doesn't it?

68
00:05:13,028 --> 00:05:15,728
You could mistake him for a real feudal lord.

69
00:05:15,728 --> 00:05:18,668
Just like a full-size traditional doll.

70
00:05:18,888 --> 00:05:21,288
You brought a tear to this old man's eye.

71
00:05:21,848 --> 00:05:25,108
So then, where's your opponent, Yoko Mizo, hiding?

72
00:05:25,348 --> 00:05:25,608
Huh?

73
00:05:29,988 --> 00:05:30,508
Yeah.

74
00:05:31,328 --> 00:05:33,168
And he looks just like...

75
00:05:33,168 --> 00:05:33,948
Let's see.

76
00:05:34,288 --> 00:05:35,408
What do you call it?

77
00:05:35,988 --> 00:05:36,508
Hmm.

78
00:05:37,908 --> 00:05:39,508
Could it be a henchman?

79
00:05:39,508 --> 00:05:41,808
Hey, stop making me sound like a side character.

80
00:05:58,668 --> 00:06:02,508
And now, Yoko Mizo, 7th Dan, has the first move.

81
00:06:04,508 --> 00:06:05,888
Pawn to 7-6.

82
00:06:09,508 --> 00:06:18,628
Next, Nikaido, 5th Dan.

83
00:06:19,588 --> 00:06:20,968
Pawn to 3-4.

84
00:06:25,388 --> 00:06:26,868
Pawn to 6-6.

85
00:06:29,288 --> 00:06:30,628
Pawn to 8-4.

86
00:06:32,888 --> 00:06:34,348
Rook to 6-8.

87
00:06:34,348 --> 00:06:40,248
Alright, next move, silver to 6-7.

88
00:06:40,788 --> 00:06:41,588
Wait, huh?

89
00:06:42,248 --> 00:06:44,508
What was I thinking?

90
00:06:45,068 --> 00:06:47,628
How could I completely forget that a lance moved up?

91
00:06:48,108 --> 00:06:49,208
What's wrong with me?

92
00:06:51,628 --> 00:06:52,348
So...

93
00:06:52,828 --> 00:06:56,948
Inhuman Shogi, you're expected to move all the pieces on the board.

94
00:06:57,068 --> 00:06:58,788
It's not a rule, but it's the goal.

95
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:01,188
It's a different type of fight, actually,

96
00:07:01,188 --> 00:07:03,668
which can make it rather easy to miss something.

97
00:07:04,348 --> 00:07:05,608
Now, what?

98
00:07:06,228 --> 00:07:07,008
Bishop, same.

99
00:07:10,508 --> 00:07:11,068
Right.

100
00:07:11,768 --> 00:07:13,108
Pawn to 3-5.

101
00:07:13,828 --> 00:07:17,688
Ah, a smart move that takes advantage of his opponent's mistake.

102
00:07:18,028 --> 00:07:19,528
Hey, that's my young master.

103
00:07:22,428 --> 00:07:25,028
It looks like I've lost.

104
00:07:25,028 --> 00:07:29,408
In the 42nd annual game of Human Shogi,

105
00:07:29,408 --> 00:07:31,648
the winner, after 96 moves,

106
00:07:31,808 --> 00:07:33,228
is Nikaido, 5th Dan.

107
00:07:33,348 --> 00:07:33,668
Congrats!

108
00:07:34,188 --> 00:07:35,608
Thank you very much, everyone.

109
00:07:36,288 --> 00:07:38,248
It's been a pleasure participating today.

110
00:07:38,368 --> 00:07:39,588
Master Harunobu!

111
00:07:39,788 --> 00:07:42,008
It was one truly incredible match!

112
00:07:42,548 --> 00:07:43,568
Good game.

113
00:07:43,688 --> 00:07:45,368
You both played very well.

114
00:07:45,768 --> 00:07:46,508
Go on.

115
00:07:46,708 --> 00:07:47,508
You deserve it.

116
00:07:47,548 --> 00:07:48,928
Have some tea, Mr. Henchman.

117
00:07:48,928 --> 00:07:49,668
It's Yoko Mizo!

118
00:07:49,988 --> 00:07:51,068
You did that deliberately!

119
00:07:54,188 --> 00:07:56,188
All right, so...

120
00:07:56,188 --> 00:07:58,488
Looks like the 100-move event is up next.

121
00:07:58,948 --> 00:08:01,808
Chairman, Nikaido, Okuyasu, and I are in it.

122
00:08:02,868 --> 00:08:03,388
Kiriyama!

123
00:08:03,688 --> 00:08:05,068
I'm counting on you, kid!

124
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:06,968
Come on, Chairman.

125
00:08:07,268 --> 00:08:08,228
You're in the program.

126
00:08:08,428 --> 00:08:09,628
You can't just run away.

127
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:12,928
Huh?

128
00:08:13,948 --> 00:08:14,508
Wait.

129
00:08:15,168 --> 00:08:18,068
I think that my stomach is beginning to hurt.

130
00:08:18,328 --> 00:08:19,788
I'm not buying that lie.

131
00:08:20,128 --> 00:08:22,608
I overheard you talking about how excited you are

132
00:08:22,608 --> 00:08:24,368
to have Grade A local beef tonight.

133
00:08:24,628 --> 00:08:27,288
And besides, all the participants are looking forward

134
00:08:27,288 --> 00:08:28,868
to beating you again this year.

135
00:08:29,588 --> 00:08:31,948
But I learned my lesson last year.

136
00:08:31,948 --> 00:08:35,468
The people of this town are surprisingly good at shogi.

137
00:08:35,828 --> 00:08:38,448
Especially the old folks from that club you formed, Shimada.

138
00:08:38,848 --> 00:08:41,108
Even that old lady there would open with a fortress

139
00:08:41,108 --> 00:08:41,828
like it's nothing.

140
00:08:42,048 --> 00:08:43,588
It's not normal, I tell you.

141
00:08:44,248 --> 00:08:46,528
I can't finish the game in two hours.

142
00:08:47,268 --> 00:08:49,388
My Grade A beef will get cold.

143
00:08:50,008 --> 00:08:50,348
Yeah.

144
00:08:50,608 --> 00:08:52,148
I heard all about that, too.

145
00:08:52,668 --> 00:08:54,848
Mr. Tsuji was complaining about it last year.

146
00:08:55,168 --> 00:08:56,488
Said they whipped him pretty hard.

147
00:08:56,908 --> 00:08:58,368
Ah, Tsuji, you say.

148
00:08:58,988 --> 00:08:59,868
That guy.

149
00:08:59,868 --> 00:09:02,148
Did you hear him at the opening ceremony?

150
00:09:06,228 --> 00:09:09,068
Good afternoon, all the people of Tendo.

151
00:09:09,348 --> 00:09:10,928
Let's be friend-o.

152
00:09:12,448 --> 00:09:13,528
I'm Takeshi Tsuji.

153
00:09:15,748 --> 00:09:18,528
It was bad.

154
00:09:18,808 --> 00:09:20,148
The locals weren't having it.

155
00:09:20,368 --> 00:09:22,448
I didn't think they'd be so put off by him.

156
00:09:22,448 --> 00:09:25,828
Of course he'd say that.

157
00:09:26,068 --> 00:09:27,448
Was there ever any question?

158
00:09:27,828 --> 00:09:31,448
If you put Mr. Tsuji on stage, he'll end up telling puns.

159
00:09:32,568 --> 00:09:33,868
It's finally time.

160
00:09:34,188 --> 00:09:36,448
Players, thank you for your cooperation.

161
00:09:37,888 --> 00:09:39,888
Everyone, thank you for your patience.

162
00:09:40,368 --> 00:09:42,988
And now, welcome to the 100 Move event.

163
00:09:43,228 --> 00:09:45,288
Here are our professional shogi players.

164
00:09:45,828 --> 00:09:47,368
Hi, everybody. Hello.

165
00:09:50,168 --> 00:09:52,308
Okoyasu, go take on the Shio No Club.

166
00:09:52,608 --> 00:09:53,688
What? No way, Chairman.

167
00:09:53,988 --> 00:09:55,748
All of these people are here to beat you.

168
00:09:56,088 --> 00:09:56,928
No, thank you.

169
00:09:57,948 --> 00:09:58,968
Oh, boy.

170
00:09:59,488 --> 00:10:00,888
Well, I guess it can't be helped.

171
00:10:01,668 --> 00:10:03,668
So, how about I go instead?

172
00:10:04,188 --> 00:10:05,208
Hey, Shimada!

173
00:10:05,708 --> 00:10:07,488
Alright, grandmas and grandpas.

174
00:10:07,728 --> 00:10:09,128
I'm not going to hold back.

175
00:10:09,488 --> 00:10:10,508
Better not, Shimada.

176
00:10:10,768 --> 00:10:12,548
Guess you won't be having dinner tonight.

177
00:10:13,168 --> 00:10:14,608
But I really like dinner.

178
00:10:15,088 --> 00:10:16,508
Well, since I came all this way,

179
00:10:16,508 --> 00:10:17,708
let's eat together.

180
00:10:22,448 --> 00:10:32,188
Oh, I see. Very good.

181
00:10:32,308 --> 00:10:33,148
That makes sense.

182
00:10:39,988 --> 00:10:41,708
So, Kiriyama 5th Dan,

183
00:10:41,828 --> 00:10:44,268
what do you think of Shimada 8th Dan's hometown?

184
00:10:45,108 --> 00:10:45,528
Hmm.

185
00:10:45,528 --> 00:10:47,688
Why does he look so familiar?

186
00:10:48,888 --> 00:10:49,648
That's right.

187
00:10:50,288 --> 00:10:52,588
I'm Izumida with the Yamagata Journal.

188
00:10:53,048 --> 00:10:54,748
He did an article on Mr. Shimada.

189
00:10:55,888 --> 00:10:56,728
Uh, right.

190
00:10:56,868 --> 00:10:59,088
Well, uh, I get the feeling

191
00:10:59,088 --> 00:11:01,948
that everyone here really supports Mr. Shimada.

192
00:11:01,948 --> 00:11:06,948
Shimada 8th Dan's actual hometown

193
00:11:06,948 --> 00:11:09,948
is more in the rural backcountry of Yamagata.

194
00:11:10,468 --> 00:11:12,088
As the population declines,

195
00:11:12,288 --> 00:11:13,668
seniors living on their own

196
00:11:13,668 --> 00:11:16,088
can get isolated in their homes in the winter

197
00:11:16,088 --> 00:11:17,268
because of the snow.

198
00:11:17,728 --> 00:11:19,908
Not wanting to leave them alone in their homes,

199
00:11:20,228 --> 00:11:23,348
Shimada created the Shiono Shogi Club.

200
00:11:25,408 --> 00:11:26,828
So, twice a week,

201
00:11:26,968 --> 00:11:29,188
a bus goes to all of the seniors' homes

202
00:11:29,188 --> 00:11:30,128
to pick them up.

203
00:11:30,128 --> 00:11:32,988
Then they play Shogi together

204
00:11:32,988 --> 00:11:34,248
at the community center.

205
00:11:34,648 --> 00:11:36,808
While some relax under kotatsu's,

206
00:11:37,048 --> 00:11:38,848
others cook big pots of food

207
00:11:38,848 --> 00:11:40,168
for everyone to enjoy.

208
00:11:40,588 --> 00:11:42,608
And when it's time for them to go home,

209
00:11:42,868 --> 00:11:44,288
the seniors can take food

210
00:11:44,288 --> 00:11:45,888
and other essentials with them,

211
00:11:45,988 --> 00:11:48,968
which Shimada generously arranges and pays for.

212
00:11:50,988 --> 00:11:52,988
He cares about each of them

213
00:11:52,988 --> 00:11:54,208
and wants to make sure

214
00:11:54,208 --> 00:11:55,868
that none of the elderly people

215
00:11:55,868 --> 00:11:58,068
in the area ever feel isolated.

216
00:11:58,068 --> 00:12:01,048
He's also responsible for making arrangements

217
00:12:01,048 --> 00:12:02,848
to sell the food and sweets

218
00:12:02,848 --> 00:12:04,328
the Shiono Club makes

219
00:12:04,328 --> 00:12:05,488
to the local vendors.

220
00:12:06,268 --> 00:12:08,988
And the best part is how all these activities

221
00:12:08,988 --> 00:12:11,348
have made the old folks feel young again.

222
00:12:11,828 --> 00:12:12,088
Huh?

223
00:12:12,568 --> 00:12:15,728
Sorry, I really didn't mean to go on like that.

224
00:12:15,868 --> 00:12:17,248
Don't worry, it's all right.

225
00:12:17,508 --> 00:12:18,688
I'm glad you told me.

226
00:12:19,688 --> 00:12:21,748
Mr. Shimada has been depressed lately.

227
00:12:21,748 --> 00:12:23,608
He's been trying to figure out

228
00:12:23,608 --> 00:12:24,848
how to apologize to everyone

229
00:12:24,848 --> 00:12:26,188
about the Shishio tournaments.

230
00:12:27,228 --> 00:12:28,308
But right now,

231
00:12:28,708 --> 00:12:30,108
seeing him smile like that

232
00:12:30,108 --> 00:12:33,488
makes me feel really happy too, you know?

233
00:12:33,928 --> 00:12:35,168
What I mean is…

234
00:12:35,168 --> 00:12:36,148
Is that how you feel?

235
00:12:36,508 --> 00:12:37,828
Oh, that's good.

236
00:12:38,108 --> 00:12:39,728
It's just that I've been covering him

237
00:12:39,728 --> 00:12:41,208
for the newspaper for so long

238
00:12:41,208 --> 00:12:43,488
that I've become totally enamored with the guy.

239
00:12:43,568 --> 00:12:44,108
I get it.

240
00:12:44,448 --> 00:12:45,248
I know what you mean.

241
00:12:45,248 --> 00:12:50,888
I see.

242
00:12:52,388 --> 00:12:53,628
Oh, do you now?

243
00:12:56,208 --> 00:12:58,668
When Mr. Izumita said that and smiled,

244
00:12:59,088 --> 00:13:00,088
he seemed so happy.

245
00:13:00,768 --> 00:13:02,368
Seeing that made me happy too.

246
00:13:04,548 --> 00:13:07,408
I felt connected to it somehow.

247
00:13:09,568 --> 00:13:11,268
And in a strange way,

248
00:13:11,868 --> 00:13:13,908
it somehow filled me with joy as well.

249
00:13:15,248 --> 00:13:20,548
Here is some homemade miso,

250
00:13:20,708 --> 00:13:21,748
a few rice balls,

251
00:13:21,908 --> 00:13:22,888
some pickled vegetables,

252
00:13:23,128 --> 00:13:24,608
a bunch of pear rice cakes,

253
00:13:24,748 --> 00:13:26,908
and some frozen dried persimmons too.

254
00:13:26,968 --> 00:13:27,708
Thank you.

255
00:13:27,888 --> 00:13:30,128
But this is way too much food as usual.

256
00:13:30,888 --> 00:13:32,908
Honestly, you folks never change.

257
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:35,268
And we never will either.

258
00:13:36,528 --> 00:13:38,308
We'll never change.

259
00:13:38,388 --> 00:13:40,788
So don't worry about it.

260
00:13:42,468 --> 00:13:44,768
There's no need to rush, Kai.

261
00:13:45,248 --> 00:13:49,748
I've been rushing so much,

262
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:50,868
I lost my head.

263
00:13:51,868 --> 00:13:54,588
How many times have I had to start over?

264
00:13:56,048 --> 00:13:58,048
I was completely lost.

265
00:13:58,888 --> 00:14:00,548
Even after all that's happened.

266
00:14:01,548 --> 00:14:03,648
That feeling won't go away.

267
00:14:03,648 --> 00:14:06,608
Hey, Mr. Shimada, the train's coming.

268
00:14:06,908 --> 00:14:07,988
Yeah, come on.

269
00:14:08,228 --> 00:14:09,388
You gotta hurry up.

270
00:14:09,948 --> 00:14:10,428
Coming.

271
00:14:11,648 --> 00:14:13,208
I guess that's that.

272
00:14:14,468 --> 00:14:16,148
I'll have to start over.

273
00:14:16,988 --> 00:14:19,548
I'll get back to work and I'll play on.

274
00:14:19,548 --> 00:14:28,388
It's gonna be scary, but let me pass through.

275
00:14:28,808 --> 00:14:30,448
Let me pass through.

276
00:14:30,448 --> 00:14:41,488
I'm not sure what to do.

277
00:14:43,988 --> 00:14:44,948
What is it?

278
00:14:45,008 --> 00:14:46,108
Everything all right, Grandpa?

279
00:14:46,608 --> 00:14:48,368
Is it about your next creation?

280
00:14:49,288 --> 00:14:49,728
Yeah.

281
00:14:50,448 --> 00:14:55,968
I'm trying to think of something new that would be good for the summer, but I feel so uninspired.

282
00:14:56,288 --> 00:14:57,248
I don't know.

283
00:14:57,868 --> 00:15:02,128
Although the Crescent Moons are great and have become Marchtown's signature suite,

284
00:15:02,588 --> 00:15:06,028
it would be nice to have at least one more showpiece for the season.

285
00:15:06,028 --> 00:15:12,928
If that's the case, then we need something special that has a name and shape that's easy to remember.

286
00:15:13,408 --> 00:15:16,808
It also needs to last long enough to be bought and given as a gift.

287
00:15:17,128 --> 00:15:18,508
Maybe a baked treat of some kind.

288
00:15:18,528 --> 00:15:20,028
Wait, hold on a second.

289
00:15:20,448 --> 00:15:25,148
It needs to stay fresh, but if it's baked, it'll wind up being too much like our Crescent Moons.

290
00:15:25,328 --> 00:15:27,168
But maybe we can go with something different.

291
00:15:27,508 --> 00:15:27,948
I know.

292
00:15:28,328 --> 00:15:29,208
Strawberry Mochi.

293
00:15:29,208 --> 00:15:31,388
It doesn't stay fresh long, but it sells.

294
00:15:32,028 --> 00:15:33,708
Strawberry Mochi, huh?

295
00:15:33,708 --> 00:15:37,788
I was surprised when it came out, but it tastes good and became very popular.

296
00:15:38,408 --> 00:15:38,868
Hmm.

297
00:15:39,588 --> 00:15:40,308
I see.

298
00:15:40,588 --> 00:15:43,868
So maybe something like Strawberry Mochi, but with a new flavor.

299
00:15:44,248 --> 00:15:45,208
Something unique.

300
00:15:45,328 --> 00:15:46,048
That would work.

301
00:15:46,568 --> 00:15:49,168
All right, Hina, what summer flavors do you like best?

302
00:15:49,288 --> 00:15:50,728
What would you fill the Mochi with?

303
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:52,048
Well, let's see.

304
00:15:52,388 --> 00:15:53,428
Apples are really good.

305
00:15:53,768 --> 00:15:54,188
Oh, yeah.

306
00:15:54,488 --> 00:15:55,388
And whipped cream!

307
00:15:56,428 --> 00:15:57,628
Whipped cream?

308
00:15:58,888 --> 00:16:00,068
Whipped cream.

309
00:16:00,068 --> 00:16:04,728
I think putting whipped cream in a Japanese-style confection would ruin the quality.

310
00:16:05,328 --> 00:16:08,308
There just isn't a place for it in our traditional desserts.

311
00:16:08,548 --> 00:16:10,868
But bean paste and whipped cream are delicious together.

312
00:16:11,088 --> 00:16:12,308
They're the perfect pairing.

313
00:16:12,628 --> 00:16:14,948
You can even add ice cream and jelly or Mochi balls.

314
00:16:15,528 --> 00:16:16,768
Well, that's true.

315
00:16:16,988 --> 00:16:19,908
All of that is pretty good when you add whipped cream on top.

316
00:16:19,908 --> 00:16:21,828
With bean paste and cream, huh?

317
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,328
That is yummy together.

318
00:16:23,328 --> 00:16:28,268
I especially love it when walking past all those lovely dessert stores in town.

319
00:16:28,508 --> 00:16:31,748
But sweet shops can be traps too, can't they?

320
00:16:33,568 --> 00:16:34,728
I'm tired.

321
00:16:35,068 --> 00:16:36,988
Want to get something sweet before heading home?

322
00:16:37,128 --> 00:16:38,148
Yeah, definitely!

323
00:16:38,848 --> 00:16:41,208
It's all right to splurge once in a while, right?

324
00:16:41,808 --> 00:16:42,288
Look!

325
00:16:42,448 --> 00:16:44,388
That one is only 350 yen.

326
00:16:45,108 --> 00:16:47,728
But I'd want to put sweet beans on top too.

327
00:16:47,888 --> 00:16:51,688
That sounds good, but if we had sweet beans, it would add up to 430 yen.

328
00:16:51,688 --> 00:16:54,368
And for the two of us, that's 860 yen.

329
00:16:54,488 --> 00:16:56,468
Oh, if you want, we can add ice cream.

330
00:16:56,728 --> 00:16:58,648
It'll only cost 100 yen more.

331
00:16:58,848 --> 00:17:00,488
We can't have dessert without ice cream.

332
00:17:00,848 --> 00:17:04,428
But if we're going to go that far, another 50 yen would get us whipped cream on top.

333
00:17:04,468 --> 00:17:06,328
Wait a minute, then we need apricots too.

334
00:17:06,548 --> 00:17:08,168
I can't have whipped cream without them.

335
00:17:08,468 --> 00:17:09,668
Then I'll have bananas.

336
00:17:10,388 --> 00:17:10,968
Ta-da!

337
00:17:11,768 --> 00:17:12,328
Cat!

338
00:17:17,848 --> 00:17:19,388
Now I feel awful.

339
00:17:19,388 --> 00:17:22,188
Why does this always happen to us?

340
00:17:22,608 --> 00:17:25,388
We spent 1610 yen on just sweets.

341
00:17:25,928 --> 00:17:27,328
I'm completely stuffed.

342
00:17:27,428 --> 00:17:28,408
I'm going to get fat.

343
00:17:28,728 --> 00:17:30,768
And I'm supposed to be the responsible one.

344
00:17:30,808 --> 00:17:32,028
I always save money.

345
00:17:32,428 --> 00:17:36,668
With all we've just spent, we could have bought days worth of chicken and made all sorts of dishes.

346
00:17:37,128 --> 00:17:40,168
It would have been enough to feed the whole family for a week.

347
00:17:41,128 --> 00:17:42,948
Sweet chops are just super scary.

348
00:17:42,948 --> 00:17:45,328
You can go crazy looking at the menu.

349
00:17:45,728 --> 00:17:47,048
And you can get fat.

350
00:17:47,368 --> 00:17:49,948
This must be our punishment for going without Mama.

351
00:17:50,428 --> 00:17:52,708
We've got to be more careful with our money this month.

352
00:17:52,848 --> 00:17:53,888
I regret it already.

353
00:17:54,568 --> 00:17:55,008
Hey!

354
00:17:55,468 --> 00:17:56,268
Stop that!

355
00:17:56,388 --> 00:17:57,128
Snap out of it!

356
00:17:57,408 --> 00:17:58,548
Did that happen recently?

357
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:01,488
I thought you were helping me come up with a new idea!

358
00:18:04,488 --> 00:18:05,448
Mama, my darling!

359
00:18:05,648 --> 00:18:06,528
How about you?

360
00:18:06,528 --> 00:18:08,708
What's your favorite mochi filling?

361
00:18:08,988 --> 00:18:10,188
What do you like?

362
00:18:17,268 --> 00:18:18,288
Mama, gal!

363
00:18:23,648 --> 00:18:24,968
She's a genius!

364
00:18:24,968 --> 00:18:28,268
Um, okay.

365
00:18:28,768 --> 00:18:29,428
It's all right.

366
00:18:29,588 --> 00:18:30,228
Calm down.

367
00:18:30,968 --> 00:18:33,048
Now, Grandpa, let's think this through.

368
00:18:33,288 --> 00:18:34,628
We'll figure it out.

369
00:18:34,808 --> 00:18:35,168
Okay.

370
00:18:35,528 --> 00:18:37,508
If we're going to make a new mochi,

371
00:18:38,268 --> 00:18:39,428
we'll need a tasty filling.

372
00:18:40,008 --> 00:18:41,848
First, red bean paste, of course.

373
00:18:42,008 --> 00:18:43,228
And green soybean paste.

374
00:18:43,348 --> 00:18:45,748
And some walnuts, matcha, apples, and strawberries.

375
00:18:46,188 --> 00:18:47,768
Oh, and some chestnuts.

376
00:18:47,928 --> 00:18:48,908
And sweet potatoes.

377
00:18:49,688 --> 00:18:51,168
And whipped cream!

378
00:18:51,968 --> 00:18:52,528
Hey!

379
00:18:52,748 --> 00:18:53,968
Not all that again!

380
00:18:53,968 --> 00:18:55,568
Our sweets are strictly Japanese!

381
00:18:56,148 --> 00:18:58,128
If I went along with your crazy ideas,

382
00:18:58,188 --> 00:18:59,528
this would turn into a cake shop!

383
00:18:59,728 --> 00:19:02,228
Don't you kids appreciate Japanese sweets anymore?

384
00:19:02,488 --> 00:19:03,288
Of course we do!

385
00:19:03,328 --> 00:19:03,968
We love them!

386
00:19:04,008 --> 00:19:04,988
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

387
00:19:05,348 --> 00:19:06,608
I can't do it!

388
00:19:06,728 --> 00:19:07,748
I can't decide!

389
00:19:07,828 --> 00:19:08,888
There's too many choices!

390
00:19:09,668 --> 00:19:12,488
Chestnut, matcha cream, strawberry, apple!

391
00:19:15,188 --> 00:19:17,448
You always want this and that!

392
00:19:17,548 --> 00:19:18,648
Why are you so greedy?

393
00:19:18,908 --> 00:19:21,508
You don't really expect me to pick just one!

394
00:19:21,848 --> 00:19:23,248
There's just so many flavors!

395
00:19:23,968 --> 00:19:24,528
Huh?

396
00:19:26,528 --> 00:19:27,848
I've got an idea!

397
00:19:28,848 --> 00:19:32,148
Here we go!

398
00:19:32,628 --> 00:19:33,468
You mean like this?

399
00:19:33,668 --> 00:19:34,288
Oh wow!

400
00:19:34,348 --> 00:19:35,148
How cute!

401
00:19:35,428 --> 00:19:36,948
It's like a snowman!

402
00:19:38,108 --> 00:19:38,988
Ha ha ha!

403
00:19:39,088 --> 00:19:39,908
I'm a genius!

404
00:19:41,268 --> 00:19:42,708
What are they called?

405
00:19:42,708 --> 00:19:44,608
Marge Town's fortunate fellows!

406
00:19:44,988 --> 00:19:47,268
They're mochi filled with different flavors of bean jam!

407
00:19:47,588 --> 00:19:49,408
When you put them together, they look like people!

408
00:19:49,788 --> 00:19:50,688
Aren't they cute?

409
00:19:51,068 --> 00:19:53,028
And they can also bring good fortune!

410
00:19:53,488 --> 00:19:56,048
So doubling the flavors means doubling the fortune!

411
00:19:56,048 --> 00:19:57,508
Mm-hmm!

412
00:19:57,508 --> 00:19:58,728
I think you're right!

413
00:19:58,808 --> 00:19:59,728
This could work!

414
00:19:59,928 --> 00:20:02,788
Two flavors of bean jam together in a set!

415
00:20:02,928 --> 00:20:03,828
And they're cute!

416
00:20:04,148 --> 00:20:05,828
Soybean paste with some whipped cream!

417
00:20:06,148 --> 00:20:07,628
Or red bean with sweet potato!

418
00:20:07,628 --> 00:20:10,608
You can make different kinds just by changing what's inside!

419
00:20:10,888 --> 00:20:13,128
It'd be nice to switch the fillings with the seasons!

420
00:20:13,468 --> 00:20:14,588
Limited time flavors!

421
00:20:15,068 --> 00:20:16,008
Chestnut in the fall!

422
00:20:16,348 --> 00:20:18,048
And strawberry cream in the spring!

423
00:20:18,368 --> 00:20:18,808
Ha ha!

424
00:20:18,808 --> 00:20:22,388
I'll tell everyone in the shop about it tomorrow!

425
00:20:23,328 --> 00:20:24,568
Gotta be positive!

426
00:20:24,908 --> 00:20:25,388
Yeah!

427
00:20:25,668 --> 00:20:26,488
How cool!

428
00:20:28,788 --> 00:20:29,588
Look mom!

429
00:20:29,788 --> 00:20:30,528
Look at this!

430
00:20:30,748 --> 00:20:31,848
I thought of a new treat!

431
00:20:31,988 --> 00:20:32,188
See?

432
00:20:33,488 --> 00:20:34,728
Don't eat me!

433
00:20:37,108 --> 00:20:38,208
Hey grandpa!

434
00:20:38,668 --> 00:20:41,248
Mom was the one that came up with the crescent moons, right?

435
00:20:41,728 --> 00:20:42,028
Huh?

436
00:20:42,348 --> 00:20:43,208
What'd you just say?

437
00:20:43,528 --> 00:20:44,508
Of course not!

438
00:20:44,848 --> 00:20:48,188
I'm the one who made the prototype, the mold, and put in the finishing touches!

439
00:20:49,768 --> 00:20:50,868
But yeah!

440
00:20:51,528 --> 00:20:55,008
The one who thought up all of the cute shapes and name was your mother!

441
00:20:55,428 --> 00:20:56,748
She was very special!

442
00:20:58,288 --> 00:20:59,348
Your mom!

443
00:20:59,748 --> 00:21:03,128
She just loved to bake and cook Japanese sweets!

444
00:21:03,428 --> 00:21:06,968
She liked to experiment in the kitchen and learn by watching others!

445
00:21:07,308 --> 00:21:10,488
She'd make her own original sweets all by herself!

446
00:21:11,008 --> 00:21:11,808
How cool!

447
00:21:13,508 --> 00:21:17,048
I really hope everyone can enjoy my fortunate fellows

448
00:21:17,048 --> 00:21:19,448
as much as they enjoy mom's crescent moons!

449
00:21:20,828 --> 00:21:22,488
I can't wait for them to try it!

450
00:21:24,108 --> 00:21:24,708
Oh yeah!

451
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:33,508
Nothing for us yet!

452
00:21:33,508 --> 00:21:34,028
Meow!

453
00:21:34,028 --> 00:21:34,328
Meow!

454
00:21:42,128 --> 00:21:42,748
Yes?

455
00:21:42,948 --> 00:21:43,428
Hello?

456
00:21:45,348 --> 00:21:46,588
Hi there, Ray!

457
00:21:49,928 --> 00:21:51,768
It's nice to hear from you!

458
00:21:54,008 --> 00:21:54,648
Hi!

459
00:21:54,788 --> 00:21:55,248
Good evening!

460
00:21:56,628 --> 00:21:59,408
So, would you like to come over for dinner?

461
00:22:00,208 --> 00:22:02,928
Um, sure. I'd love to.

462
00:22:05,008 --> 00:22:07,468
Long time no see, Rei! How have you been?

463
00:22:07,668 --> 00:22:09,428
Was the human shogi match fun?

464
00:22:09,908 --> 00:22:12,788
Yeah, it was. It rained, but it was still fun.

465
00:22:13,148 --> 00:22:14,568
Oh, what have you got there?

466
00:22:15,028 --> 00:22:17,548
Oh, yeah. It's food from my mentor's hometown.

467
00:22:17,928 --> 00:22:18,868
He's from Yamagata.

468
00:22:19,348 --> 00:22:22,128
He'd never finish it all, so he gave the rest of it to me.

469
00:22:22,548 --> 00:22:23,868
Oh, how wonderful!

470
00:22:23,868 --> 00:22:26,228
Please, come and join us, Rei!

471
00:22:26,228 --> 00:22:32,108
Today, Rei brought over all kinds of snacks and goodies from his trip to Yamagata.

472
00:22:33,348 --> 00:22:38,148
And Akari was super excited about all of the fresh dishes he shared with us.

473
00:22:38,668 --> 00:22:43,388
And after dinner, we all got to try the fortunate fellows I came up with for dessert.

474
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:49,988
Also, this is a secret, but when I grow up, I'd like to make Japanese sweets for a living.

475
00:22:50,848 --> 00:22:54,788
And someday, maybe I can make new sweets and run the shop with Grandpa.

476
00:22:56,228 --> 00:22:57,468
Love, Hinata!

477
00:22:57,468 --> 00:22:57,488
Love, Hinata!

478
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:35,311
Why not? It's the truth, isn't it?

479
00:24:35,431 --> 00:24:36,431
Now don't falter!

480
00:24:37,051 --> 00:24:39,571
But why? Is Shogi really that dull?

481
00:24:40,391 --> 00:24:43,371
Hey, there are limits to making snap decisions, too.

482
00:24:44,351 --> 00:24:47,611
As you can see, we're harvesting natto.

483
00:24:48,371 --> 00:24:50,171
Hey, can we eat together?

484
00:24:51,291 --> 00:24:53,631
I'm definitely a guy who can bring out the sun.

485
00:24:53,751 --> 00:24:56,271
For next year's human Shogi, it's going to be sunny.

486
00:24:56,491 --> 00:24:58,691
Don't miss the next March comes in like a lion.

487
00:25:01,011 --> 00:25:30,991
Thank you.

